Medians over the runs. E121's targets: <10 ms on the keystroke path, <500 ms to errors.
CPU is the whole server process (every thread) from the edit to the analysis's publish for the file, and to idle; instructions are user-space, every thread, edit to idle; wall includes the debounce and the machine's load. Keystroke requests are asked before the analysis lands; idle requests after it. A pause row rests until the server has been quiet for its pause; every other row resumes after 0.4 s.
